1v4y|v|To disunite; to divide; to disconnect; to sever; to part in any manner. ; To come between; to keep apart by occupying the space between; to lie between; as, the Mediterranean Sea separates Europe and Africa. ; To set apart; to select from among others, as for a special use or service. ; To part; to become disunited; to be disconnected; to withdraw from one another; as, the family separated.	o:t78,49,3;1unf,36,9;1vql,34,1;1o05,21,4;1zf0,21,8;l6s,19,4;1m06,13,5;4ir,6,1~1unf,36,9;1zf0,21,8;1m06,13,5;l6s,19,4;1o05,21,4;t78,49,3;4ir,6,1;1vql,34,1	s:26bd,38,61~26bd,38,61	d:ekj,34,12;p73,30,4;de1,16,3~ekj,34,12;p73,30,4;de1,16,3
