1vf7|n|of Set ; The act of one who, or that which, sets; as, the setting of type, or of gems; the setting of the sun; the setting (hardening) of moist plaster of Paris; the setting (set) of a current. ; The act of marking the position of game, as a setter does; also, hunting with a setter. ; Something set in, or inserted. ; That in which something, as a gem, is set; as, the gold setting of a jeweled pin.	a:1n5m,32,10;er,23,22;hnu,17,12;2aq5,15,4;14m7,14,1;48q,14,4;v56,10,7;t0o,9,3;hlg,6,6~er,23,22;hnu,17,12;1n5m,32,10;v56,10,7;hlg,6,6;48q,14,4;2aq5,15,4;t0o,9,3;14m7,14,1	v:e9b,47,7;dpy,35,2~e9b,47,7;dpy,35,2	V:afm,28,10~afm,28,10	n:dby,43,4;1ewy,19,5;1wlx,13,5;1rl5,8,1;26cl,6,4;1zop,2,1;1bbk,1,10;1wx7,1,3~1bbk,1,10;1ewy,19,5;1wlx,13,5;26cl,6,4;dby,43,4;1wx7,1,3;1rl5,8,1;1zop,2,1	N:c35,18,6~c35,18,6
